[{:db/id "q-102568/selection/3d4a06a736cc478ad4d703e27c143f8e9ec982fcd79a9f4c120c46756cdad10a" :answer/id #uuid "51261d45-18aa-565e-bd5e-0de7772a7f6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{5}{(x+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102568/selection/d2bbf49c1f738350edd12d25dd89800df5b275b4f929376f8d0ced881a41603c" :answer/id #uuid "6fc02512-1729-5caf-ba08-55e1876ec02c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x-1}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}-\\frac{4}{(x+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102568/selection/43760ef485ca3f1acbe1cb5bcf0fa1741a54ab89ed3d3d8397a03d08c968ecb6" :answer/id #uuid "2de8007c-efb4-50d2-9fac-a556222eba6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102568/selection/f965c8dbdd4d20df6297cec9f43c97e41e83143abfc66ca0ddb91487317888fe" :answer/id #uuid "9083c75f-a0c5-5f36-b62c-9fbf205ed4ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x-2}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}-\\frac{2}{(x+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102568/selection/638ef1c10941b73dc3e7e79fa6f8f903157cbb57c8577f480cee9c8c010d4487" :answer/id #uuid "c9cfb5b7-a323-5137-8dd9-6980395cee4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102568/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b91643-5355-5918-9758-59dee221b7f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102568/selection/638ef1c10941b73dc3e7e79fa6f8f903157cbb57c8577f480cee9c8c010d4487" :answer-field/choices ["q-102568/selection/3d4a06a736cc478ad4d703e27c143f8e9ec982fcd79a9f4c120c46756cdad10a" "q-102568/selection/d2bbf49c1f738350edd12d25dd89800df5b275b4f929376f8d0ced881a41603c" "q-102568/selection/43760ef485ca3f1acbe1cb5bcf0fa1741a54ab89ed3d3d8397a03d08c968ecb6" "q-102568/selection/f965c8dbdd4d20df6297cec9f43c97e41e83143abfc66ca0ddb91487317888fe" "q-102568/selection/638ef1c10941b73dc3e7e79fa6f8f903157cbb57c8577f480cee9c8c010d4487"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102568" :question/id #uuid "ed503c06-b57c-5cdc-af73-5c39124e5788" :question/math-academy-id "q-102568" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{4{x}^{2}+10x+6}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}+10x+6}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)(x+3)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{C}{(x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+3x+4$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $\\frac{4{x}^{2}+10x+6}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)(x+3)}$ and get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+10x+6=(Ax+B)(x+3)+C({x}^{2}+3x+4).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-3)^{2}+10(-3)+6 & =(A(-3)+B)(-3+3)+C((-3)^{2}+3(-3)+4) \\\\ 36-30+6 & =4C \\\\ 12 & =4C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}+10(0)+6 & =(A(0)+B)(0+3)+C({0}^{2}+3(0)+4) \\\\ 6 & =3B+4C \\\\ 6 & =3B+4(3) \\\\ 3B & =6-12 \\\\ B & =\\frac{-6}{3} \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1)^{2}+10(1)+6 & =(A(1)+B)(1+3)+C({1}^{2}+3(1)+4) \\\\ 20 & =4A+4B+8C \\\\ 20 & =4A+4(-2)+8(3) \\\\ 4A & =20+8-24 \\\\ A & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=1,B=-2,$ and $C=3.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+10x+6}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)(x+3)}=\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}+3x+4)}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102568/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102568"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102574/selection/807570684c57ff25a3735d2145ed8dc9f501e9bfbb016ef4438ad4eec189dc83" :answer/id #uuid "7304a0de-2e97-5fac-b324-7bf43228622b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}-\\frac{4}{(x-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102574/selection/32eecb4a057ded44731b37a2ef994f935b3a884d756058d6aee8a9a32667818e" :answer/id #uuid "33c3ab64-1998-5867-bfd1-a50d2fcb9d74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{3}{(x-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102574/selection/7629f2d18041fef6d150bd33aec25cb803568b522670d38ddc649d3d25f5b225" :answer/id #uuid "fcd6d45f-9ded-520b-b23e-252f9516a4d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}-\\frac{3}{(x-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102574/selection/2c88f4ec07c8226e2127865c060f52027e0552ce429e1f0f0ee89d59a7c41a73" :answer/id #uuid "eab7f8c6-e90b-59f9-9582-572d13da153b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x-3}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102574/selection/f8f5ade1059154229479c5cc7e154334055aa406586c38558791f05a9cf4a3ca" :answer/id #uuid "8f477b23-cc79-59c6-a024-c5289aa51a5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102574/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "350000aa-cc96-585b-90c7-198678f19cbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102574/selection/2c88f4ec07c8226e2127865c060f52027e0552ce429e1f0f0ee89d59a7c41a73" :answer-field/choices ["q-102574/selection/807570684c57ff25a3735d2145ed8dc9f501e9bfbb016ef4438ad4eec189dc83" "q-102574/selection/32eecb4a057ded44731b37a2ef994f935b3a884d756058d6aee8a9a32667818e" "q-102574/selection/7629f2d18041fef6d150bd33aec25cb803568b522670d38ddc649d3d25f5b225" "q-102574/selection/2c88f4ec07c8226e2127865c060f52027e0552ce429e1f0f0ee89d59a7c41a73" "q-102574/selection/f8f5ade1059154229479c5cc7e154334055aa406586c38558791f05a9cf4a3ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102574" :question/id #uuid "0d6aaf9d-b896-5612-9d3e-9a2c1d285c38" :question/math-academy-id "q-102574" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-29x+34}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)(x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{x}^{2}-29x+34}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)(x-3)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}-4x+5$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}-4x+5)(x-3)$ and get\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-29x+34=(Ax+B)(x-3)+C({x}^{2}-4x+5).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(3)^{2}-29(3)+34 & =(A(3)+B)(3-3)+C({3}^{2}-4(3)+5) \\\\ 63-87+34 & =2C \\\\ C & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-29(0)+34 & =(A(0)+B)(0-3)+C({0}^{2}-4(0)+5) \\\\ 34 & =-3B+5C \\\\ 34 & =-3B+5(5) \\\\ 3B & =25-34 \\\\ B & =\\frac{-9}{3} \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(1)^{2}-29(1)+34 & =(A(1)+B)(1-3)+C({1}^{2}-4(1)+5) \\\\ 12 & =-2A-2B+2C \\\\ 12 & =-2A-2(-3)+2(5) \\\\ 2A & =-12+6+10 \\\\ A & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=2,B=-3,$ and $C=5.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-29x+34}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)(x-3)}=\\frac{2x-3}{({x}^{2}-4x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x-3)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102574/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351326/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer/id #uuid "873d0196-7d12-54d8-873f-8fcafdad832e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351326/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1167940f-f8af-53d3-9608-53c4a11b55dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351326/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer-field/choices ["q-351326/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351326/field-2/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437" :answer/id #uuid "c9a9fcbb-0956-5f3b-af49-06a82980ec40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351326/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fba3f53-6ecb-5f02-9210-5fbcb22b241c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351326/field-2/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437" :answer-field/choices ["q-351326/field-2/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351326/field-3/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "88808e5e-044c-5693-8818-e1b8d2c67ad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351326/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0eea284c-78e7-51dd-bdb6-1a3e49da4a80" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351326/field-3/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-351326/field-3/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351326" :question/id #uuid "0de8cf89-d134-59d7-b539-d68786c14110" :question/math-academy-id "q-351326" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-{x}^{2}+7x+1}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-{x}^{2}+7x+1}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}}$\\,x\\,+$\n{{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $13({x}^{2}+9)$ |  | $13(x-2)$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$, $B$, and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{2}+7x+1}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{C}{x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)$ gives\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+7x+1=(Ax+B)(x-2)+C({x}^{2}+9).\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(2)^{2}+7(2)+1 & =C(4+9) \\\\ 11 & =13C \\\\ C & =\\frac{11}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(0)^{2}+7(0)+1 & =(A(0)+B)(0-2)+\\frac{11}{13}((0)^{2}+9) \\\\ 1 & =-2B+\\frac{99}{13} \\\\ -2B & =-\\frac{86}{13} \\\\ B & =\\frac{43}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(1)^{2}+7(1)+1 & =(A(1)+\\frac{43}{13})(1-2)+\\frac{11}{13}((1)^{2}+9) \\\\ 7 & =-A-\\frac{43}{13}+\\frac{110}{13} \\\\ -A & =\\frac{24}{13} \\\\ A & =-\\frac{24}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{2}+7x+1}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-2)} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{24}{13}x+\\frac{43}{13})}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{(\\frac{11}{13})}{x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24\\,x+43}{13({x}^{2}+9)}+\\frac{11}{13(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351326/field-1" "q-351326/field-2" "q-351326/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351326"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
